  "limits": [
    "No physical iOS data-protection/lock-state, real disk-full, SIGKILL or power-loss proof.",
    "Initial hydration and the existing synchronous compatibility methods remain synchronous; async write preparation and commit/hydration use the serial worker.",
    "GC is explicit and conservative: it reclaims authenticated unreferenced receipt bytes while retaining metadata provenance and unknown entries; no metadata compaction.",
    "Portable Snapshot and v1-v3 exports retain base64 hydration; no streamed memory or capacity increase claim.",
    "Legacy migration happens on the next successful mutation/publication-identity write, not an eager startup rewrite.",
    "A failed async commit conservatively closes the store until reload, even when the old generation was restored."
  ]
